From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:45:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: Refuse to connect a ring while a dead ring of the
 VBD drains

When a frontend resets, tapdisk keeps the old ring as dead while its
requests are in flight, and until now accepted the reconnected ring
straight away. Both rings feed the same VBD queues with nothing
ordering them. A write that is stuck on the dead ring (a storage stall,
or tapdisk's own retry of a write that failed with EAGAIN) can land
after the guest's newer write to the same sectors through the new ring:
a lost update. Barriers and flushes are counted per ring, so a flush on
the new ring does not wait for it either.

tapdisk_xenblkif_connect() now returns EBUSY while the VBD has a dead
ring, after the EALREADY check so that a restarted tapback still sees
an existing connection as such. tapback retries the connection until
the dead ring is gone (previous commit).

Any dead ring is enough to refuse, not only one with writes queued:
it keeps the check trivial. With "tapdisk: Do not take requests off a
dead ring", a dead ring takes no new requests and only drains, so the
refusal always ends; without it, the dead ring can still take requests
the frontend left on it, which delays the reconnection.

Cost: the guest does not get its ring connected until the old ring's
requests are done; it waits in Initialised. A tapback that does not
know EBUSY gives up on the connection instead, so tapback must be
updated with or before tapdisk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/td-blkif.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/td-blkif.c b/drivers/td-blkif.c
index 9884e32e..7c561c80 100644
--- a/drivers/td-blkif.c
+++ b/drivers/td-blkif.c
@@ -522,6 +522,19 @@ tapdisk_xenblkif_connect(domid_t domid, int devid, const grant_ref_t * grefs,
         return -EALREADY;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * A dead ring of this VBD still has requests in flight. Requests of a new
+     * ring would not be ordered against them: a write of the dead ring could
+     * land after a newer write to the same sectors, and a flush on the new
+     * ring would not wait for it. Refuse the connection until the dead rings
+     * are gone; tapback retries it.
+     */
+    if (tapdisk_vbd_contains_dead_rings(vbd)) {
+        DPRINTF("refusing to connect domid=%d, devid=%d: a dead ring of the "
+                "VBD still has requests in flight\n", domid, devid);
+        return -EBUSY;
+    }
+
     err = tapdisk_xenio_ctx_get(pool, &td_ctx);
     if (err) {
         /* TODO log error */
